# The app's own pages load the app. Anything else that isn't a file (a missing photo, a mistyped
# path) gets 404.html, a copy of index.html made by `npm run build`, with a real 404 status, so a
# missing image is a 404, not the page, cached as a photo. (The app sends a mistyped path home.)
# The target is / rather than /index.html: Pages strips .html, so that would loop and be ignored.
/collage    /  200
/room/*     /  200
/collage/*  /  200
